WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:06.196
You want a black T-shirt, in your size, with the right balance of price, quality and sustainability.

2
00:00:06.356 --> 00:00:08.929
Green Choice starts with what matters to you.

3
00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:15.531
A long answer can still leave you comparing products, checking sources, and asking again.

4
00:00:15.691 --> 00:00:22.391
Our exploratory audit found uneven support for finding information and assessing its reliability.

5
00:00:23.483 --> 00:00:30.395
Try our interactive shopping demo, powered by an AI model and the fixed product profiles from our research.

6
00:00:30.555 --> 00:00:35.149
Compare two options, ask a follow-up question, and explore the trade-offs.

7
00:00:36.217 --> 00:00:45.719
In this example, Product One costs three hundred Danish kroner. Product Three costs four hundred, with a higher study-defined sustainability level.

8
00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:54.471
These are fictional research profiles. Ethical Consumer guides provide separate background reading, not verification of these products.

9
00:00:55.550 --> 00:01:00.318
In our shopper study, price and quality mattered alongside sustainability.

10
00:01:00.478 --> 00:01:06.354
Additional explanation showed no reliable overall improvement in the primary outcomes.

11
00:01:06.514 --> 00:01:09.217
That is why the whole experience needs testing.

12
00:01:10.283 --> 00:01:16.064
Independent food-label research suggests sustainability information can carry value.

13
00:01:16.224 --> 00:01:19.170
It cannot tell us what someone would pay for Green Choice.

14
00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:27.951
For retailers, the next step is a focused pilot connecting product data, evidence, and an existing shopping experience.

15
00:01:28.111 --> 00:01:32.655
We will measure useful results, source quality, time, and willingness to pay.

16
00:01:33.717 --> 00:01:37.940
Have a product catalogue, a research question, or a shopping challenge?

17
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.450
Build the next shopping experience with us.

